CC — open-source projects it is built on

CC would not exist without the projects below. Thank you to their authors.


1. Cockpit Tools
   https://github.com/jlcodes99/cockpit-tools
   Author: jlcodes
   License: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/)

   CC started from Cockpit Tools 1.2.2 (a local build, 1.2.2-local.20260930) and
   keeps its Codex features: account management, the local API service, wake-up
   tasks, multiple app instances, session management and model providers. CC changed them: the other platforms
   were removed, the interface was redesigned, and Claude features were added.
   Cockpit Tools in turn credits other projects in its README, among them
   CLIProxyAPI (below) and CC Switch (https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch),
   whose provider presets it drew on.


2. CC Same
   https://github.com/songkeys/cc-same
   Author: Songkeys
   License: MIT (text below; also in crates/cc-same-core/LICENSE)

   CC's Claude Desktop session sync engine (crates/cc-same-core) is CC Same's,
   taken at version 0.1.13. CC changed it to run its own background agent and
   log, to share an installed CC Same's data folder until the user lets CC take
   over syncing and then keep its own copy, and to work alongside CC Same
   without the two syncing at the same time. Changes are marked "CC:" in the
   source.


3. CLIProxyAPI
   https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI
   Authors: Luis Pater, Router-For.ME
   License: MIT (text below; also in sidecars/cockpit-cliproxy/cdk/CLIProxyAPI/LICENSE)

   The local API proxy bundled with CC (cc-proxy), by way of Cockpit Tools.


